                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_01\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit initializes the field `runningBatchKey` in `BddRunContext.java` with a default value:\n\n    - private Optional<String> runningBatchKey;\n    + // must be initialized for jbehave-junit-runner\n    + private Optional<String> runningBatchKey = Optional.of(\"batch-1\");\n\nThe fix message explains that jbehave-junit-runner builds the JUnit execution tree before any actual story execution happens, and it knows nothing about Vividus batches. Because of this, `getRunningBatchKey()`/`getRunningBatch()` can be called before `putRunningBatch()` is ever invoked, and since `runningBatchKey` was left uninitialized (null `Optional` reference), calling `.orElseThrow(...)` on it throws a NullPointerException instead of the intended `IllegalStateException`.\n\nTracing the field back through the candidates:\n- candidate_01 is the commit that creates `BddRunContext.java` from scratch (new file). It introduces the field exactly as:\n      private Optional<String> runningBatchKey;\n  with no initializer, and immediately uses it in `getRunningBatch()`:\n      String batchKey = runningBatchKey.orElseThrow(...);\n  This is the very first appearance of the buggy, uninitialized field.\n- candidate_02 does not touch `BddRunContext.java`/`runningBatchKey` at all.\n- candidate_03 refactors `getRunningBatch()` to extract a `getRunningBatchKey()` method, but the field declaration itself is untouched (still uninitialized).\n- candidate_04 shows the field declaration only as unchanged context while other parts of the batch-storage subsystem are refactored \u2014 the uninitialized field is inherited unchanged.\n- candidate_05 removes `getRunningBatch()`/`batchStorage` (unrelated cleanup) but again leaves `runningBatchKey` uninitialized as context.\n- candidate_06 is actually the fix commit itself (adds the default `Optional.of(\"batch-1\")` initializer and comment), matching `fix_commit_diff.txt` exactly.\n\nSince the uninitialized field was present from the moment the class was created and every intermediate candidate merely inherited it without addressing the initialization, candidate_01 is the commit that introduced the bug.\n"
                }
              }
